> Time: 1450207164 / Tue, 15 Dec 2015 19:19:24 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=43563&start=10&SessionId=7a8551a585a07cbaa9d5f86d27b4aee2
> User Mrsloiseau (285543)
Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d6f9b2dd6fd3a179b90cb0f2920ecc76","RawContent":"We are making MIB invites as well - hopefully they will be done this weekend, and I&#039;ll post pics. They loo really great, so far. \n \n We didn&#039;t use plastic bottles - we used the Bud Lite with Lime beer bottles, and removed the labels. We thought about using plastic ones - specifically the new plastic bottles that Bacardi Breezers come in, but we didn&#039;t want to drink that many breezers - too sweet! and also I didn&#039;t like the way the tops of the plastic bottles looked. \n \n We are using sand from the playground up the road - although we considered going to the beach and getting beach sand. We baked the sand in the oven for a bit first to dry it out. \n \n Our shells are just from the dollar store - two bags of shells, and most of them are small enough to fit into the bottle mouths. I also had a bunch of glass stones that we&#039;ll probably throw in for some colour. \n \n We are staining regular computer paper with tea to age it, then burning the edges to make it look more message-in-a-bottlish. I found that computer paper rolled the easiest, and costs a lot less than other paper. Although if I can find a paper that looks aged for cheap, I&#039;ll totally use that. \n \n To make the bottles look nicer, I have glued twine around them - it looks nicer than a plan bottle. The twine is long enough that it is what we are tying around the invitations so they can be pulled out easily. I also have attached a small charm to each bottle on the bottleneck. \n \n We are buying wine corks for 10 cents a cork at a wine-making store - then since they don&#039;t quite fit into beer bottles, we are shaving them down slightly so that they will fit tightly. \n \n Again- this is my project for this weekend - I&#039;ll post pics when they are done!! :)","Attachments":[],"Id":887760,"PostDate":1255719955,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                We are making MIB invites as well - hopefully they will be done this weekend, and I'll post pics. They loo really great, so far. <br \/> <br \/> We didn't use plastic bottles - we used the Bud Lite with Lime beer bottles, and removed the labels. We thought about using plastic ones - specifically the new plastic bottles that Bacardi Breezers come in, but we didn't want to drink that many breezers - too sweet! and also I didn't like the way the tops of the plastic bottles looked. <br \/> <br \/> We are using sand from the playground up the road - although we considered going to the beach and getting beach sand. We baked the sand in the oven for a bit first to dry it out. <br \/> <br \/> Our shells are just from the dollar store - two bags of shells, and most of them are small enough to fit into the bottle mouths. I also had a bunch of glass stones that we'll probably throw in for some colour. <br \/> <br \/> We are staining regular computer paper with tea to age it, then burning the edges to make it look more message-in-a-bottlish. I found that computer paper rolled the easiest, and costs a lot less than other paper. Although if I can find a paper that looks aged for cheap, I'll totally use that. <br \/> <br \/> To make the bottles look nicer, I have glued twine around them - it looks nicer than a plan bottle. The twine is long enough that it is what we are tying around the invitations so they can be pulled out easily. I also have attached a small charm to each bottle on the bottleneck. <br \/> <br \/> We are buying wine corks for 10 cents a cork at a wine-making store - then since they don't quite fit into beer bottles, we are shaving them down slightly so that they will fit tightly. <br \/> <br \/> Again- this is my project for this weekend - I'll post pics when they are done!! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><strong>21 people + Bride & Groom booked!!<\/strong><br><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;80\/st\/20100414\/e\/Beth+and+Jon%27s+Wedding%21\/dt\/1\/k\/8e20\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...8e20\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"bholthof@connect.carleton.ca","IpAddress":"","GroupId":5,"GroupName":"Banned","JoinDate":1247552705,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-219399.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bholthof","Id":219399,"Name":"bholthof","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"edb4fe919eb4862700e6aa3bedcfb722","RawContent":"What a great idea!","Attachments":[],"Id":887855,"PostDate":1255722772,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                What a great idea!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10747;130\/st\/20100122\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/bd26\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...bd26\/event.png<\/a><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span>[url=<\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/weight-loss\/w20NyYs\/%5D\">http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/weight-loss\/w20NyYs\/]<\/a><br \/>\n<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/t\/w20NyYs\/weight.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...yYs\/weight.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"meghankawa@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1233367763,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-214468.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"isaidyes","Id":214468,"Name":"isaidyes","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"05bb637ab5f33a2b224f14b509a22267","RawContent":"I purchased my plastic bottles at Michaels during the summer (haven&#039;t seen any more right now). They came in packs of 6 and I used a 50% off coupon every time ($3.45). It comes with the cork and paper. I&#039;m getting sand and shells from a friend and my MIL is getting me labels for the outside of them. I just happened to have ribbon in our wedding colors which I will use to attach the paper to the cork. So total cost $0.58\/each plus my time and ink. Have not completed yet but will post a pic when done.","Attachments":[],"Id":888386,"PostDate":1255736672,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I purchased my plastic bottles at Michaels during the summer (haven't seen any more right now). They came in packs of 6 and I used a 50% off coupon every time ($3.45). It comes with the cork and paper. I'm getting sand and shells from a friend and my MIL is getting me labels for the outside of them. I just happened to have ribbon in our wedding colors which I will use to attach the paper to the cork. So total cost $0.58\/each plus my time and ink. Have not completed yet but will post a pic when done.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;130\/st\/20100504\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/9e4d\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...9e4d\/event.png<\/a><br><br><br><br><span>36 people + Bride & Groom are coming to Cuba!!!<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"krista_lehnhardt@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1225849279,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-212533.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":151,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"K'osh","Id":212533,"Name":"K'osh","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"41d42349f98ed2985fb791d5c3b42eb4","RawContent":"&lt;font face=\"Garamond\"&gt;good luck with all the projects, ladies. I also wanted to do the MIB invites, but after speaking to mom she suggested them as favors. As since we&#039;re having a small guest list it kinda works. I was getting them from &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=\"http:\/\/www.hansonellis.com\"&gt;Wedding Favors, Party Favors &amp;amp; Personalized Gifts, Bridal Shower Favors | HansonEllis.com&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/font&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":889161,"PostDate":1255801440,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <font face=\"Garamond\">good luck with all the projects, ladies. I also wanted to do the MIB invites, but after speaking to mom she suggested them as favors. As since we're having a small guest list it kinda works. I was getting them from <a href='http:\/\/www.hansonellis.com' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Wedding Favors, Party Favors & Personalized Gifts, Bridal Shower Favors | HansonEllis.com<\/a><\/font>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/global.theknot.com\/tools\/tickers\/tt25913.aspx\">http:\/\/global.theknot.com\/tools\/tickers\/tt25913.aspx<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"lily17bear@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1238312442,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-216255.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"lily17bear","Id":216255,"Name":"lily17bear","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"850436d9314c9f25b8b5c3195872479d","RawContent":"I&#039;d like to add fragrance so when you remove the cork it smells like beach (or coconut, etc). Anyone know where to buy these oils?","Attachments":[],"Id":920686,"PostDate":1257967788,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I'd like to add fragrance so when you remove the cork it smells like beach (or coconut, etc). Anyone know where to buy these oils?\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"geminigem615@aol.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1231215388,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-213622.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":75,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"KimmyG","Id":213622,"Name":"KimmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a3052b7c62ca1084d45d1c57f1afa33b","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;KimmyG&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;I&#039;d like to add fragrance so when you remove the cork it smells like beach (or coconut, etc). Anyone know where to buy these oils?&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;We did coconut in ours and we got out ours at a flea market but I bet you could find them at Michaels or Walmart. Our guests said that really made the invitations because it reminded them of the beach!","Attachments":[],"Id":920746,"PostDate":1257969992,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>KimmyG<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">I'd like to add fragrance so when you remove the cork it smells like beach (or coconut, etc). Anyone know where to buy these oils?<\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div>We did coconut in ours and we got out ours at a flea market but I bet you could find them at Michaels or Walmart. Our guests said that really made the invitations because it reminded them of the beach!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Our Honeymoon In Ireland!!<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"jkcz0702@gmail.com","IpAddress":"75.99.176.34","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1208067675,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-209088.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":79,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Jen_S","Id":209088,"Name":"Jen_S","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8c45da575f350de9888e46636fd487cd","RawContent":"Thanks for the tip, JKCZ. I didn&#039;t find anything at Kroger so I will check your suggestions. \n \n Do you dip the cork in oil, spray the invitations, or put a few drops in the bottle? What works best?","Attachments":[],"Id":920776,"PostDate":1257970941,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Thanks for the tip, JKCZ. I didn't find anything at Kroger so I will check your suggestions. <br \/> <br \/> Do you dip the cork in oil, spray the invitations, or put a few drops in the bottle? What works best?\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"geminigem615@aol.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1231215388,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-213622.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":75,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"KimmyG","Id":213622,"Name":"KimmyG","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5678cb28ec6c9bc298c0ef5ae301b495","RawContent":"Hi everyone. I don&#039;t have the time to make these on my own (we are also remodeling a home) but I found great ones with starfish from Hanson &amp;amp; Ellis. They also personalized the bottle with our names &amp;amp; wedding date. I have only showed them to a few people &amp;amp; they just love them!\n \n Chrissy","Attachments":[],"Id":922753,"PostDate":1258069053,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hi everyone. I don't have the time to make these on my own (we are also remodeling a home) but I found great ones with starfish from Hanson & Ellis. They also personalized the bottle with our names & wedding date. I have only showed them to a few people & they just love them!<br \/> <br \/> Chrissy\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Chrissy & Jeremiah's Blog with Pictures...<\/span><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.brilliant.tc\/2010\/05\/chrissy-jeremiah-island-escape\/\">http:\/\/www.brilliant.tc\/2010\/05\/chri...island-escape\/<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"christinambucko@aol.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1258064938,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223252.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":100,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Girasole","Id":223252,"Name":"Girasole","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":false,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8c0e310f9981b98fe5ec16604d803dab","RawContent":"For the scented oil - I just used the fragrance oils from the Body Shop. I put a drop or two on the cork &amp;amp; let it sink in.","Attachments":[],"Id":922773,"PostDate":1258069689,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                For the scented oil - I just used the fragrance oils from the Body Shop. I put a drop or two on the cork & let it sink in.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><strong>21 people + Bride & Groom booked!!<\/strong><br><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;80\/st\/20100414\/e\/Beth+and+Jon%27s+Wedding%21\/dt\/1\/k\/8e20\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...8e20\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"bholthof@connect.carleton.ca","IpAddress":"","GroupId":5,"GroupName":"Banned","JoinDate":1247552705,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-219399.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"bholthof","Id":219399,"Name":"bholthof","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":43563,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"dd01b93933ba1bd42f97e2ecfffa5aba","RawContent":"Adding the scent is such an awesome idea....I may have to steal it for my own...thanks ladies.","Attachments":[],"Id":924313,"PostDate":1258155426,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Adding the scent is such an awesome idea....I may have to steal it for my own...thanks ladies.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;130\/st\/20100504\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/9e4d\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...9e4d\/event.png<\/a><br><br><br><br><span>36 people + Bride & Groom are coming to Cuba!!!<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"krista_lehnhardt@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1225849279,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-212533.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":151,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"K'osh","Id":212533,"Name":"K'osh","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":22,"TotalPages":3,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":20},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
